{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120462","id":3900733428,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7ogHf0","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120462","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120462.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120462.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120462","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120462/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120462/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120462/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f71d40aed38b5eced29de1f8c57b87571256d916","number":120462,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Allow reading multiple data chunks per frame in a single-threaded `HTTPRequest`","user":{"login":"NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev","html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem(s) solved by this PR\r\n\r\n- Closes #120425 \r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nWhen `use_threads = false` on a `HTTPRequest,` incoming data gets processed on the main thread. Right now, only one chunk gets read per frame, which means throughput is effectively capped at `download_chunk_size * FPS`, which can be problematic (see the linked issue for more details)\r\n\r\nThis PR lets multiple chunks be processed within a single frame.\r\n\r\nI also added a `read_time_limit` property that limits how much time can be spent reading data per frame (only applies when `use_threads = false`, it's not used otherwise). Without a limit like this, a fast connection could end up stalling the main for even seconds. At least one read still always happens per frame regardless of the limit.\r\n\r\nHere is some data from a project running at 20 FPS, downloading a 16 MiB file on a simulated 10 MB/s network (localhost with a python server):\r\n| `download_chunk_size` | 4 KB | 65 KB | 512 KB |\r\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|\r\n| 4.7.stable | 205 s | 13 s | 1.9 s |\r\n| **This PR** | **1.85 s** | **1.85 s** | **1.85 s** |\r\n\r\n## Author disclosure\r\n\r\nI used Claude to discuss possible approaches, though honestly most of its suggestions were awful, and to review the changes for mistakes before pushing. \r\nAll the code is mine.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/m